close and who's out.","published":"2026-11-17T15:58:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503628/cfp-playoff-2026-bubble-watch-week-third-ranking","type":"Story","byline":"Heather Dinich","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Breaking down the major futures for the Big Ten, from the Heisman to the CFP","description":"Let's evaluate whether a standout performance on a three-loss team and a 10-0 team are real or a mirage in the Big Ten.","published":"2026-11-17T13:02:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50504671/college-football-heisman-trophy-cfp-futures-betting-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"Pamela Maldonado","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Arkansas State tells Butch Jones he's out at end of year","description":"Arkansas State has informed football coach Butch Jones that he's out at the end of the season, sources told ESPN's Pete Thamel on Monday night.","published":"2026-11-17T02:45:08.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50506952/sources-butch-jones-arkansas-state-coach","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Top 25 betting lines: UGA big faves over Gamecocks, Vols slim favorites vs. LSU","description":"This week's odds and FPI predictions for South Carolina-Georgia, Tennessee-LSU and more.","published":"2026-11-16T23:15:08.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50498153/2026-college-football-week-12-top-25-betting-lines-odds","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Illinois may turn to third-string QB Boyd after Houser injury","description":"Illinois might turn to third-string quarterback Carson Boyd this week against No. 15 Iowa after starter Katin Houser suffered a broken nose Friday at UCLA that required surgery.","published":"2026-11-16T21:42:38.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50504718/illinois-turn-third-string-qb-boyd-houser-injury","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4685314/sebastian-cheeks","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sebastian_Cheeks"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Sebastian Cheeks","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sebastian_Cheeks","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:38:20Z","intro":"Sebastian Cheeks (born February 6, 2004) is an American college football outside linebacker for the Wisconsin Badgers. He previously played for the North Carolina Tar Heels.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Cheeks attended Evanston Township High School in Evanston, Illinois, where he played linebacker and running back. As a sophomore he recorded two interceptions which he returned for touchdowns over his first four games before suffering a season-ending injury. Cheeks was selected to play in the 2022 All-American Bowl, where he was named the All-American Bowl's Man of the Year. A four-star recruit, he committed to University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Cheeks played the 2022 and 2023 season with North Carolina, recording four tackles over eight games. After the 2023 season, he entered the transfer portal and committed to the University of Wisconsin Madison. In his first year at Wisconsin in 2024, he played in 11 games and had 12 tackles with two sacks. Cheeks started three of 12 games in 2025, recording 24 tackles and three sacks. He returned to Wisconsin as a starter in 2026."}]}}